@startuml mvp_session_state
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title MVP session and alarm transitions — owner decisions 11/12 October
[*] --> Boot
Boot --> Idle : software-observable startup checks pass
Boot --> DA : essential functionality fails
Idle --> Listening : Start / Heart or Lung
Idle --> Portal : long press >= 2 s, or automatically when no Wi-Fi credentials are stored / Idle network lease, open hotspot
Portal --> Idle : confirm / PATCH Device.patient + readback
Portal --> Idle : cancel or timeout / no change
Listening --> Measuring : Heart session begins / freeze context
Listening --> Idle : Stop in Lung / mute, no BPM or send
Measuring --> Idle : Stop before 15 s / cancel, no send
Measuring --> Analysing : Stop at or after 15 s / mute, finalize
Analysing --> Sending : valid BPM + configured prerequisites
Analysing --> ReportingError : invalid BPM + validated error contract + prerequisites
Analysing --> Idle : Wi-Fi unconfigured / no send or Wi-Fi error
Analysing --> Idle : delivery prerequisites fail / latch normal fault
Sending --> Idle : accepted + matching readback
Sending --> Idle : failed or unverified after 3 retries / latch normal fault
ReportingError --> Idle : error report verified / no numeric BPM
ReportingError --> Idle : report failed after 3 retries / latch normal fault
note as NormalFaultIndication
  Normal-fault latch is independent of workflow state.
  Separate manual acknowledgement clears only the indication.
  Preserve the current workflow; no implicit Start.
end note
DA --> Boot : full device restart only
note right of Analysing
  Start = Busy, visible activity.
  No cancellation or queued Start.
end note
note right of Sending
  Same Busy rule during both send paths.
  Exclusive network lease; audio stopped.
end note
note bottom of Measuring
  Reject mode/patient/context changes with a normal fault.
  Keep frozen session identity and current session.
  Normal Wi-Fi/BPM faults preserve functioning audio.
  Normal-fault indication is latched separately from workflow;
  acknowledgement does not change an active workflow.
end note
note bottom of DA
  Any detected dangerous/essential-function fault -> DA.
  Mute; invalidate incomplete work; latch until restart.
  A button cannot restore operation.
end note
@enduml
